{
 "name": "poly_triple_reflex_divergence",
 "description": "Which diagonals a triangulation cuts on a ring with a REFLEX corner. The vertex sets match completely in both cells -- no vertex is created or moved by either engine -- and the entire divergence is in which vertices make a triangle. On the pentagon (0,0,0) (4,0,0) (4,0,4) (2,0,1) (0,0,4), whose reflex corner is (2,0,1), the reference's fan leaves every triangle inside the ring, while ours emits (0,0,0)-(4,0,0)-(4,0,4), a triangle that CONTAINS the reflex corner: the output overlaps itself. The hexagon case is the same shape of result on a 6-gon whose reflex corner is (2,0,1) -- our first triangle (0,0,0)-(3,0,0)-(3,0,3) contains it too. 2 of 3 and 2 of 4 face rings differ respectively.",
 "source": "Reference side: headless command-port capture of the triangulate command (dirty-geometry sweep, task 1123, cases tri_reflex_mid / tri_reflex_hex). vibe3d side: live drive of this build.",
